    <template v-if="locale==='en'">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>This statement applies to the website entscheidsuche.ch and to the MCP interface at mcp.entscheidsuche.ch, through which AI assistants such as ChatGPT or Claude can search the collection.</p>
      <p>When you use the website, your requests are transmitted to entscheidsuche.ch. For technical reasons, the transmitted data include your IP address as well as the documents you open and the searches you run. These data are processed by our processors <a href="https://www.cyon.ch">cyon.ch</a> and <a href="https://erbguth.ch">erbguth.ch</a> (both Switzerland) and <a href="https://www.pansoft.de">pansoft.de</a> (Germany); erbguth.ch uses <a href="https://www.netcup.de">netcup.de</a> (Germany) as a sub-processor. The data are not disclosed to any other third parties. We do not keep individual statistics; we only carry out a rudimentary log file analysis to monitor the number of requests and the load on our systems and, where necessary, to respond to attacks. Log files are deleted after 3 months or earlier. In the event of specific attacks or for troubleshooting, we reserve the right to log in more detail temporarily and to trace requests.</p>
      <p>This website does not use cookies. Your browser may store the files of the web application in its cache. We do not evaluate this for profiling or any other purpose.</p>
      <p>The AI search uses a language model on a server of our own, hosted at <a href="https://www.pansoft.de">pansoft.de</a>. Your searches are not transmitted to providers of language models such as Anthropic or OpenAI.</p>
      <p>When you use the MCP interface from ChatGPT, Claude or another AI assistant, the assistant sends the request to us. If it runs at the provider, we receive the provider's IP address; if it runs as a program on your device, we receive your IP address. We also receive the name and version of the requesting program, the function called and the search query or the identifier of the requested decision. The wording of the search query is determined by the assistant; it may contain information that you have given the assistant in the conversation. We log the time, IP address, requesting program, function called and status of the request, but not the wording of the search queries (except occasionally for troubleshooting). No account is required, and we do not attribute requests to any person. The response containing the decisions found goes to the assistant that requested it; beyond that, we do not disclose any data to its provider. We have no influence on what the provider of the assistant does with your input and with our responses.</p>
      <p>If you are a sponsor or member of entscheidsuche.ch, we store your data for membership administration and accounting. With your consent, we also list you as a supporter on our website; you can withdraw this consent at any time. We delete the data as soon as we no longer need them for these purposes and no statutory retention obligation remains.</p>
      <p>This data processing is governed by the Swiss <a href="https://www.fedlex.admin.ch/eli/cc/2022/491/en">Federal Act on Data Protection</a> (FADP, SR 235.1) and, in special cases, possibly also by the <a href="https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32016R0679&from=EN">General Data Protection Regulation</a> (GDPR).</p>
      <p>We base the operation of the website and the interface, and logging for security and load monitoring, on our overriding private interest (GDPR: legitimate interest, Art. 6(1)(f)). Membership administration is based on the membership or sponsorship relationship (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR), accounting on legal obligations (Art. 6(1)(c)) and listing as a supporter on your consent (Art. 6(1)(a)).</p>
      <p>Data protection law gives you certain rights as a data subject. You can request access to the data we process, their rectification or erasure, and the delivery or transfer of the data you have provided to us, and you can object to the processing.</p>
      <p>The controller is the association Verein entscheidsuche.ch, 3000 Bern, Switzerland, <a href="mailto:info@entscheidsuche.ch">info@entscheidsuche.ch</a>. You are free to contact the <a href="https://www.edoeb.admin.ch/edoeb/en/home.html">Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner</a> (FDPIC). Where the GDPR applies, you also have the right to lodge a complaint with a competent data protection supervisory authority in the European Union.</p>
